<h2>Double Selection Sort</h2>
<p>
    Double Selection Sort is a variation of Selection Sort 
    that finds the largest element in the array in addition to the smallest. 
    Then, it swaps both the largest element with the last element, 
    and the smallest element with the first.
    <br>
    <br>
    Because Double Selection Sort swaps two elements each loop, 
    it always finishes twice as quickly as Selection Sort.
</p>